# acceptance-mutation-manifest-end

# Spec §4.1 (Steps: Advance, Complete, Undo), §4.4 (`pasoAlCompletar`),
# §5.4 and §7. `currentStep` is the number of the step the task is on (without the
# field, step 1). «Hecho» takes it to the next step and «Paso anterior» to the
# previous one; «Hecho» on the last step completes the task like the checkbox.
# "the current step of the task is N" leaves the task already on step N.
Feature: Current step

  # Current step 1
  # «Hecho» moves to the next step and does not complete the task.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 1
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    And the current step of the task is <current>
    When I tap Hecho on <tap>
    Then the task is on step <current_stored>
    And the task has no completions

    Examples:
      | steps                                                       | current | tap                 | current_stored  |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 1      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 2               |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 2      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 3               |

  # Current step 2
  # «Hecho» on a step that is not the last does not open an undo notice.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 2
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    When I tap Hecho on <tap>
    And I query the notice on <now>
    Then there is no notice

    Examples:
      | steps                                  | tap                 | now                 |
      | Llenar la regadera, Regar los helechos | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 2026-11-13T10:00:01 |

  # Current step 3
  # «Paso anterior» goes back to the previous step; on step 1 it does not go past the first.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 3
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    And the current step of the task is <current>
    When I tap Paso anterior
    Then the task is on step <current_stored>

    Examples:
      | steps                                                       | current | current_stored  |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 3      | 2               |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 2      | 1               |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 1      | 1               |

  # Current step 4
  # «Hecho» on the last step completes the task like the checkbox: it adds the
  # completion and opens its notice.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 4
    Given a relative recurring task Regar every <every> <unit>
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    And the current step of the task is <current>
    When I tap Hecho on <tap>
    And I query the notice on <now>
    Then the task is completed
    And the notice offers to undo the completion of Regar from <completed_stored>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | steps                                  | current | tap                 | now                 | completed_stored    |
      | 2    | dias   | Llenar la regadera, Regar los helechos | 2      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 2026-11-13T10:00:01 | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 |

  # Current step 5
  # The checkbox does the same: same completion and same notice.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 5
    Given a relative recurring task Regar every <every> <unit>
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    And the current step of the task is <current>
    When I tap the task checkbox on <tap>
    And I query the notice on <now>
    Then the task is completed
    And the notice offers to undo the completion of Regar from <completed_stored>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | steps                                  | current | tap                 | now                 | completed_stored    |
      | 2    | dias   | Llenar la regadera, Regar los helechos | 2      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 2026-11-13T10:00:01 | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 |

  # Current step 6
  # Completing with the checkbox, on whichever step, returns the task to step 1 and
  # the completion stores the step it was on.
  Scenario Outline: Current step 6
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the steps of the task are <steps>
    And the current step of the task is <current>
    When I tap the task checkbox on <tap>
    Then the task is on step 1
    And the last completion of the task saves step <step_stored>

    Examples:
      | steps                                                       | current | tap                 | step_stored   |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 1      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 1             |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 2      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 2             |
      | Separar la ropa blanca, Poner el lavarropas, Tender la ropa | 3      | 2026-11-13T10:00:00 | 3             |

  # Current step 7
  # Completing with «Hecho» on the last step also returns to step 1 and stores
